1
00:01:28,787 --> 00:01:30,403
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:01:31,812 --> 00:01:33,545
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:01:33,826 --> 00:01:40,185
اَلْحَمْدُ لله  وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

4
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:43,233
This is session number two,

5
00:01:43,698 --> 00:01:51,064
we'll carry on In Sha Allah Ta'ala(اِنْ شَاء الله تعالى) with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) in Makkah, we are still in Makkah.

6
00:01:52,991 --> 00:02:02,035
We talked about his Islam in the last session and the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ for him,

7
00:02:03,238 --> 00:02:07,347
اَلَلَّهُمَّ اَعِزَّ الْاِسْلَامَ بِأحَبِّ الرَّجُلَيْنِ اِلَيْكََ

8
00:02:08,486 --> 00:02:18,948
O Allah! Give Islam strength, and power through the most beloved of the two men to You,

9
00:02:19,738 --> 00:02:24,047
Amr Ibn Hisham(عمرو بن هشام) or Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Allahعزُّوْجل chose Umar(عمر).

10
00:02:25,428 --> 00:02:33,108
So, Umar(عمر) became Muslim and he grew into Islam to become the second greatest after Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه,

11
00:02:33,549 --> 00:02:36,441
while Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) chose the other course

12
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:39,052
and that is to be the Fir’auon(فرعون), of this Ummah(امة).

13
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:45,137
لِكُلٍّ وِجْهَةٌ هُوَ مُوَلِّيْها

14
00:02:45,546 --> 00:02:47,834
Everyone chooses a path.

15
00:02:50,616 --> 00:02:53,579
Now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) being the man he is,

16
00:02:54,742 --> 00:02:57,590
he didn’t want the event of his Islam to go un-noticed.

17
00:03:00,717 --> 00:03:03,494
You know, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was a man for the Ummah(اُمَة).

18
00:03:04,861 --> 00:03:12,689
Some people; you know, they want to do their Salah(صلاة) and do their small individual Ibadaat(عبادات)

19
00:03:12,769 --> 00:03:23,645
and stay out of trouble, stay out of Islamic work, don’t do anything, just pray, and do your fasting and be calm, and don’t be noticed,

20
00:03:24,015 --> 00:03:25,785
that's not Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

21
00:03:27,325 --> 00:03:29,608
Some people they just care about themselves, and their family,

22
00:03:29,629 --> 00:03:34,513
as long as I am alright, and my family is alright, then everything is good, everything is okay.

23
00:03:35,629 --> 00:03:37,316
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wasn't such a person.

24
00:03:38,129 --> 00:03:42,344
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) saw that Muslims were been tortured, he wants to be like them.

25
00:03:43,221 --> 00:03:46,327
He saw that, they are being persecuted, he wants to be like them.

26
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:53,436
He cared for the Ummah(امة) and that's why Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was a statesman by nature.

27
00:03:54,995 --> 00:03:56,933
He had the virtues of a Khalifah(خليفه).

28
00:03:57,451 --> 00:04:00,271
Because he was very, very concerned with the Ummah(امة)

29
00:04:01,078 --> 00:04:04,525
he was a man for the Ummah(امة), what pleases them, pleased him

30
00:04:05,171 --> 00:04:09,289
and what displeases them, displeased him.

31
00:04:09,786 --> 00:04:13,376
And that's why, when Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه appointed him Khalifah(خليفه),

32
00:04:13,912 --> 00:04:17,290
that's in fact, that's the statement that Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) made.

33
00:04:17,516 --> 00:04:20,744
He said: He is a man who is pleased when the Ummah(امة) is pleased

34
00:04:21,026 --> 00:04:23,224
and he is displeased when the Ummah(امة) is displeased.

35
00:04:24,004 --> 00:04:28,604
Umar(عمر) wasn't a selfish person, who is only caring about himself and his direct family,

36
00:04:28,813 --> 00:04:30,346
like many of the Muslims today are.

37
00:04:32,047 --> 00:04:35,545
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن الخطاب) wanted to join the Ummah(امة) in their happiness and in their pain.

38
00:04:36,362 --> 00:04:40,113
When he saw Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) crying, he came and he said:

39
00:04:40,416 --> 00:04:41,688
Tell me, why are you crying?

40
00:04:42,109 --> 00:04:47,292
 If it makes me cry otherwise, I will force myself to cry.

41
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,888
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want his Islam to go un-noticed.

42
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:57,565
So, where does he go, which house does he choose to go to?

43
00:04:58,522 --> 00:04:59,364
The house of Abu Jahal(ابوجهل).

44
00:05:01,662 --> 00:05:04,140
He goes to the house of Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) and knocks his door.

45
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:08,102
Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) opens the door and says; Welcome Ibn Al-Khattab(ابن الخطاب)! Welcome!

46
00:05:11,193 --> 00:05:12,956
Because he didn't know that he became Muslim yet.

47
00:05:14,039 --> 00:05:20,634
And they used to love Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) because of his dedication to the persecution of the Muslims.

48
00:05:21,448 --> 00:05:23,354
So, he said: Welcome Son of Al-Khattab(ألخطاب),

49
00:05:24,332 --> 00:05:28,832
Umar Ibn Khattab(عمربن خطاب) said: I became a Muslim, for your information.

50
00:05:30,849 --> 00:05:33,436
Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) said: What! He said: I have became Muslim.

51
00:05:33,508 --> 00:05:35,002
 Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) said: Don’t do so!

52
00:05:35,218 --> 00:05:36,137
Umar(عمر) said: Well I did!

53
00:05:38,863 --> 00:05:40,927
Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) slammed the door in his face.

54
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,302
Umar(عمر) said:

55
00:05:42,323 --> 00:05:43,122
مَا هَذَا بِشَيْ

56
00:05:43,183 --> 00:05:45,207
This is nothing, this is not, what I am looking for?

57
00:05:45,944 --> 00:05:48,805
Because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to be like the rest of the Ummah(امة)

58
00:05:48,872 --> 00:05:54,372
but no one in their sane Mind in Quraish(قريش), no matter how much they hate Islam

59
00:05:54,556 --> 00:05:59,361
was willing to take over the task of torturing Umar(عُمَر) even Abu Jahal(ابوجهل).

60
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:02,525
Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) did not want to deal with it, so he just closed the door.

61
00:06:04,203 --> 00:06:08,781
Umar(عمر) went to another house, knocking the door, welcome son of Al-Khattab(الخطاب)

62
00:06:09,030 --> 00:06:10,174
I became a Muslim.

63
00:06:10,571 --> 00:06:11,389
He said: Don’t do so!

64
00:06:11,413 --> 00:06:12,533
لَاتَفْعَلْ ،

65
00:06:12,966 --> 00:06:13,660
فَعَلْتْ

66
00:06:13,841 --> 00:06:16,108
I did so, he closes the door.

67
00:06:17,532 --> 00:06:20,609
So, there was somebody, who was watching what Umar(عمر) was doing.

68
00:06:20,679 --> 00:06:21,921
He went to Umar(عمر) and he said:

69
00:06:22,332 --> 00:06:24,812
It seems that you want people to know that you have became a Muslim?

70
00:06:24,832 --> 00:06:25,545
He said: Yes!

71
00:06:25,908 --> 00:06:27,521
He said: Do you see that man over there?

72
00:06:28,823 --> 00:06:31,944
Go to him and tell him that you have became Muslim and that's all what you need.

73
00:06:33,090 --> 00:06:36,722
He was pointing towards Jameel Bin Mu'ammar Al-Jum'hi(جميل بن معمر الجمهي)

74
00:06:37,472 --> 00:06:40,437
Jameel Bin Mu’ammr(جميل بن معمر) is a man, who cannot hold any water in his mouth,

75
00:06:41,425 --> 00:06:45,106
he was a mobile transmitter, a living broadcasting station.

76
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,781
So, he goes to him, and he says:

77
00:06:48,805 --> 00:06:50,488
يَا جَمِيْل لَقَدْ اَسْلَمْتُ

78
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:53,475
O Jameel(جميل), I have became a Muslim.

79
00:06:54,908 --> 00:06:58,816
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر), said: I was watching my father.

80
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:02,516
He Said: When he told Jameel(جميل) that he became Muslim,

81
00:07:03,167 --> 00:07:07,824
Jameel(جميل) immediately, stood up, without saying anything, he just stood up, sprang up,

82
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:14,028
dragged his Izaar(إزار) and walking briskly towards Al-Ka’aba(ألكعبه), where everybody is meeting,

83
00:07:14,675 --> 00:07:18,043
and then he says: Ya Quraish(يا قريش)! O people of Quraish(قريش)!

84
00:07:18,373 --> 00:07:22,093
Umar(عمر) embraced Islam, Umar(عمر) embraced Islam, Umar(عمر) embrace Islam.

85
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:25,711
The news was all over, breaking news all over Makkah.

86
00:07:26,048 --> 00:07:28,216
That's all, what Umar(عمر) needed to do, is to tell Jameel(جميل).

87
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:34,553
In fact, the narration says, that Jameel(جميل) wasn’t saying that Umar(عُمَر) was Muslim.

88
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,781
 He was saying Saba'a(صبأ)’

89
00:07:36,053 --> 00:07:41,175
and Saba'a(صبأ) was a derogatory term, the people of Quraish(قريش) used to use when somebody would become Muslim.

90
00:07:41,854 --> 00:07:46,108
So, Umar(عمر) was following the Jameel(جميل) trying to correct the information

91
00:07:46,332 --> 00:07:49,093
but when it gets on the front page of a newspaper, it's too late.

92
00:07:50,317 --> 00:07:54,123
Jameel(جميل) was just running all over, saying Saba'a Umar(صبا عمر), Saba'a Umar(صبا عمر)

93
00:07:54,147 --> 00:07:56,199
and Umar(عمر) is trying to correct the information, he's saying,

94
00:07:56,289 --> 00:07:57,820
بَلْ اَسْلَمْت، بَلْ اَسْلَمْتُ

95
00:07:58,379 --> 00:07:59,420
but there is nothing you could do.

96
00:08:00,974 --> 00:08:03,188
Now, Jameel(جميل) did it for Umar(عمر).

97
00:08:03,957 --> 00:08:11,071
The mobs just attacked from every direction and Umar(عمر) is, in between them fighting for himself

98
00:08:11,484 --> 00:08:14,736
and they are attacking him and he is getting hits from every side.

99
00:08:16,670 --> 00:08:17,856
What does, Umar(عمر) do?

100
00:08:18,746 --> 00:08:21,638
He grabs Ut'bah Bin Rabiya(عتبة بن ربيعه), who is one of their noble men

101
00:08:22,016 --> 00:08:26,444
throws him to the ground sits on top of him and then he sticks his fingers in his eyes.

102
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:30,886
So, Utba’ah(عتبة) screams and then everybody backs off.

103
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:37,208
Abdullah(عبدالله) said: So when he released Utba’ah(عتبه) and he walked away the mob attacked him again.

104
00:08:38,331 --> 00:08:39,449
فَجَعَلَ كُلَّمَا

105
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:42,404
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله إبن عمر) says; Whenever, the mob would attack him,

106
00:08:42,661 --> 00:08:49,150
he would grab the most noble man, he sees in front of him and stick his fingers in his eyes, until they back off.

107
00:08:49,413 --> 00:08:51,419
 And that kept on happening again and again.

108
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:58,142
He said: Eventually Umar(عمر) could not fight any further.

109
00:08:58,598 --> 00:09:00,198
People are attacking him from every direction.

110
00:09:00,236 --> 00:09:03,952
So, he just sat down, while people were hitting him and then he said:

111
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:12,582
وَاللهِ لَوْ كُنَّا ثَلَاثَ مِائَة لَتَرَكْنَهَا لَكُمْ اَوْ تَرَكْتُمُوْهَالَنَا

112
00:09:13,672 --> 00:09:20,177
If we were but three hundred strong, you would either leave it for us, or we would leave it for you!

113
00:09:21,093 --> 00:09:22,971
And this was a very Prophetic Statement.

114
00:09:24,563 --> 00:09:28,830
What Umar(عمر) was saying is, if we were three hundred strong,

115
00:09:29,262 --> 00:09:32,602
if the Muslims were three hundred strong, we would fight you

116
00:09:32,979 --> 00:09:35,943
and either you leave Makkah or we leave it for you.

117
00:09:36,726 --> 00:09:41,413
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the order of Jihad(جهاد) was given, Qitaal(قتال),

118
00:09:41,925 --> 00:09:46,498
and the first army to meet Al-Kuffr(الكفر) was three hundred and thirteen, in Badr(بدر).

119
00:09:48,213 --> 00:09:52,931
So, as if Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was waiting for it, but the numbers were not ready yet.

120
00:09:54,188 --> 00:09:56,806
We are gonna fight you, but we were few.

121
00:09:56,884 --> 00:10:02,106
And the narration says that Muslims were about forty in Makkah, when Umar(عمر) became Muslim.

122
00:10:04,019 --> 00:10:06,917
Allah o Alam(الله اعلم), if that includes the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) of Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه) or not.

123
00:10:08,223 --> 00:10:14,627
Because the majority of Muslim actually made Hijrah(حجرة) to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه).

124
00:10:21,644 --> 00:10:28,152
Umar(عمر) went to Daar-Ul-Arqam(دار الارقم) and he asked Rasool Allah ﷺ, he says;

125
00:10:28,819 --> 00:10:32,474
أ لَسْنَا عَلَى الْحَقِّ اِنْ حَيِيْنَا وَاِنْ مِتْنَا

126
00:10:33,676 --> 00:10:37,364
Aren’t we on the right path, whether we live or die?

127
00:10:38,345 --> 00:10:39,576
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

128
00:10:41,072 --> 00:10:42,674
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر إبن الخطاب) said:

129
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:45,321
فَلِمَ الْإخْتِفَاءُ اِذَاً؟

130
00:10:45,714 --> 00:10:47,592
Then why, should we hide?

131
00:10:49,382 --> 00:10:54,255
Why should our Islam be, underground, why are we hiding?

132
00:10:56,037 --> 00:11:05,358
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ agrees with Umar(عمر) and he arranges the Muslims in two ranks

133
00:11:07,658 --> 00:11:11,446
and Rasool Allah ﷺ is standing between these two ranks,

134
00:11:12,268 --> 00:11:16,582
and one rank is headed by Umar(عُمَر) and the other by Hamza(حمزه).

135
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:23,053
And they marched down the streets of Makkah declaring,

136
00:11:23,454 --> 00:11:27,482
أشْهَدُاَنْ لَّأ اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله وَ أشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُوْلَ الله

137
00:11:28,296 --> 00:11:31,096
That was the public declaration of Islam in Makkah

138
00:11:31,663 --> 00:11:34,257
and it happened when Umar(عمر) and Hamza(حمزه) became Muslims.

139
00:11:34,657 --> 00:11:40,523
And the difference in time between their Islam according to one narration was three days.

140
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:46,219
The narrator says; When they reached to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

141
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:49,470
and the people of Quraish(قريش) saw Umar(عمر) and Hamza(حمزه),

142
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,869
اَصَابَتْهُمْ كَآبَة لَمْ تُصِبْهُمْ قَطْ

143
00:11:53,373 --> 00:11:55,274
They were depressed, like never before.

144
00:11:58,032 --> 00:12:03,347
Because now, they've seen strength that Allah has given to Islam through Hamza(حمزه) and Umar(عُمَر).

145
00:12:05,868 --> 00:12:13,813
And that's the day, in which Umar(عمر) was given the name Al-Farooq(اَلْفَارُوْقْ) by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

146
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:22,477
Al-Farooq(اَلْفَارُوْقْ), the Criterion, he is the criterion of Haqq(حق) and Batil(باطل).

147
00:12:23,570 --> 00:12:27,812
He is the criteria that separated between the truth and falsehood.

148
00:12:28,349 --> 00:12:33,207
Al-Farooq(اَلْفَارُوْقْ) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) this name was given to him by Muhammadﷺ.

149
00:12:38,154 --> 00:12:42,826
The Islam of Umar(عمر) had great impact on the early Islamic Movement.

150
00:12:44,091 --> 00:12:46,195
Abdullah Ibn Masood رضي الله عنه says;

151
00:12:46,784 --> 00:12:53,370
مَا زِلْنَا اَعِزَّةْ مُنْذُ اَسْلَمَ عمر وَلَقَدْ رَأيْتَنَا وَمَا نَسْتَطِيْعُ اَنْ نَطُوْفَ بِالْبَيْتِ

152
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:58,638
حَتَّى اَسْلَمَا عمر فَلَمَّا اَسْلَمَ قَاتَلْنَاهٌمْ حَتَى تَرَكُوْنَ فَصَّلَّيْنْا وَطُفْنَا

153
00:12:58,999 --> 00:13:02,932
He said: We became powerful when Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim,

154
00:13:03,409 --> 00:13:08,424
before we were not able to even make a Tawaf(طواف) around the house of Allah or Pray.

155
00:13:08,710 --> 00:13:15,946
When he became Muslim we fought them, until they allowed us to Pray and make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka’aba(ألكعبه).

156
00:13:17,701 --> 00:13:18,491
He also says;

157
00:13:18,883 --> 00:13:26,311
كَانَ الاِسْلَامُ عمر فَتْحاً وَهجْرَتُه’ نَصْراً وَإمَارَتُه رَحْمَهَ

158
00:13:27,050 --> 00:13:31,441
وَلَقَدْ رَاَيْتَنَا وَمَا نَسْتَطِيْعُ أن نصَلِّى وَنَطُوْفَ بِالْبَيْتِ حَتَّى اَسْلَمَ عمر

159
00:13:31,792 --> 00:13:34,909
فَلَمَّا اَسْلَمَ قَاتَلْنَاهُمْ حَتَّى تَرَكُوْنَا نُصَلِّى

160
00:13:35,473 --> 00:13:38,007
He said: The Islam of Umar(عُمَر) was an opening

161
00:13:39,733 --> 00:13:46,061
and his Hijrah(هجرة) was a victory, and his reign was mercy,

162
00:13:47,897 --> 00:13:52,022
and we weren't able to pray publically, until he became Muslim.

163
00:13:53,264 --> 00:13:54,507
Suhaib Ar-Romi(صهيب الرومى) says;

164
00:13:55,553 --> 00:14:00,799
لَمَّا اَسْلَمَ عمر ابن الخطاب رضى الله عنه ظَهْرَالْاِسْلَامْ وَدُعِيَ إلِيْهِ عَلَانِيَّةَ

165
00:14:01,176 --> 00:14:07,912
وَجَلَسْنَا حَوْلَ الْبَيْتِ حِلَقًّا وَطُفْنَا بِالْبَيْتِ وَانْتَصَفْنَا مِمَّنْ غَلَظَ عَلَيْنَا وَرَدَدْنَا عَلَيْهَ

166
00:14:08,637 --> 00:14:11,622
When Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim Islam became public

167
00:14:12,908 --> 00:14:19,241
and we used to invite to Islam publically, and we use to sit in circle around the House of Allah

168
00:14:19,665 --> 00:14:22,113
and we use to make Tawaf(طواف) around the House of Allah

169
00:14:22,505 --> 00:14:26,311
and we started getting even, with the ones, who oppressed us.

170
00:14:28,363 --> 00:14:32,596
All of that because of the Islam of one man, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

171
00:14:34,135 --> 00:14:38,148
According to As-Sayuti(السيوطي) the age of Umar(عُمَر) when he became Muslim was twenty seven years old,

172
00:14:38,713 --> 00:14:45,793
which is younger than the earlier narration which would be in his thirties

173
00:14:45,851 --> 00:14:52,236
 but that’s the rough estimate of the age of the Umar(عُمَر), when he became Muslim, so he was young.

174
00:14:58,418 --> 00:14:59,375
WHAT ABOUT HIS HIJRAH(هجرة)?

175
00:15:01,196 --> 00:15:06,090
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said: Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told me,

176
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:12,412
that every Muslim made Hijrah(هجرة) secretely except Umar(عُمَر).

177
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:21,451
When he wanted to make Hijrah(هجرة), he hung his sword on his neck

178
00:15:23,773 --> 00:15:31,212
and he threw his bow over his shoulder, and he had a baton hanging from his waist,

179
00:15:32,278 --> 00:15:36,272
and he has his hand full of arrows, fully loaded.

180
00:15:37,931 --> 00:15:43,145
And then he walked to Al-Haram(الحرم) to Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه) and he made Tawaf(طواف).

181
00:15:43,379 --> 00:15:45,944
Now, all the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were sitting around Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه)

182
00:15:46,108 --> 00:15:47,412
Umar(عُمَر) was making a Tawaf(طواف).

183
00:15:47,436 --> 00:15:49,781
Now, the key word that Ali(علي) says:

184
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,083
مُتَمَكِّنا

185
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:51,834
with the confidence.

186
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:58,831
You know, because sometimes you could be going to a fight and you are putting up a strong face, while inside you are trembling,

187
00:15:58,893 --> 00:16:01,912
and you are saying: Yea! Yea! It's alright! It's fine! I am ready for it! I am ready for it!

188
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:03,259
And inside you are shaking.

189
00:16:03,824 --> 00:16:07,790
But Ali(علي) said: Mutamakinan(متمكناً), he was so confident and at ease, about it.

190
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,354
فَطَافَ مُتَّمَكِّنًاَ

191
00:16:09,378 --> 00:16:11,654
He made Tawaf(طواف) around the House with confidence.

192
00:16:12,949 --> 00:16:17,084
And then he stands behind the Maqaam-e-Ibraheem(مقام ابراهيم) and he prays.

193
00:16:18,421 --> 00:16:19,696
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

194
00:16:19,898 --> 00:16:23,326
The leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were sitting in circles around Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه).

195
00:16:24,211 --> 00:16:31,023
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) goes to those circles, one by one and he stands on top of every circle, and he says;

196
00:16:31,851 --> 00:16:32,738
شَاهَتُ الْوُجُوْهَ

197
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:35,580
May these faces be disfigured!

198
00:16:36,523 --> 00:16:39,095
وَلَا يُرْغِمُ اللهُ إلَّا هَذِهِ الْمَعَاطِسْ

199
00:16:39,310 --> 00:16:42,305
May Allahعَزّ وجَلّ humiliate these noses in the dirt!

200
00:16:43,251 --> 00:16:46,837
And then, he did not even use the word noses which is Aanf(أنْف), he said Ma’atis(معاطس)

201
00:16:47,206 --> 00:16:50,694
which is like, he is telling them the organ which you sneeze with.

202
00:16:52,682 --> 00:16:54,481
He is making, even fun of their noses, he said:

203
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:55,903
 هَذِهِ الْمَعَاطِسْ

204
00:16:56,029 --> 00:16:56,966
and then he said:

205
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:03,441
مَنْ اَرَادَ أَنْ يُثْكِلَ اُمَّهّْ

206
00:17:04,259 --> 00:17:11,511
The one, who wants his mother to be bereaved, and his wife to be a widowed

207
00:17:12,150 --> 00:17:16,248
and his children to be orphaned, come and meet me behind that valley.

208
00:17:17,954 --> 00:17:20,842
If you want your mother to cry for the loss of her son

209
00:17:21,322 --> 00:17:25,500
and your wife to live as a widow and your children to be orphans,

210
00:17:25,805 --> 00:17:27,492
come and meet me behind that valley.

211
00:17:29,202 --> 00:17:32,204
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: No body stood up

212
00:17:32,454 --> 00:17:37,274
except some of the fools of Makkah and he taught them, a very good lesson, before they went back home.

213
00:17:40,627 --> 00:17:45,800
Only Umar(عُمَر) made Hijrah(هجرة) publically, everyone else made it in hiding.

214
00:17:50,561 --> 00:17:53,912
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had made an appointment with two of his friends.

215
00:17:54,633 --> 00:18:00,381
Ayaash Ibn Abi Rabi’a(عيَّاش اِبن ابي ربيعه) and Hisham Ibn Al-Haris(هشام ابن حارث)

216
00:18:01,361 --> 00:18:03,876
that they are gonna meet in this place outside of Makkah

217
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:08,154
and they are gonna be accompanied on the journey to Madina.

218
00:18:10,104 --> 00:18:13,537
And they said: We meet at this place

219
00:18:14,406 --> 00:18:19,998
if you do not show up by this time, it means that something happened, you were arrested or something

220
00:18:20,486 --> 00:18:22,723
so whoever, is there would leave.

221
00:18:24,051 --> 00:18:29,463
So, at the appointed time Umar(عُمَر) and Ayaash(عياش) were there, Hisham(هشام) wasn't.

222
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:35,443
And Hisham(هشام) was arrested and Umar(عُمَر) says:

223
00:18:35,695 --> 00:18:37,333
فُتِنَ فَافْتُتِنْ

224
00:18:38,162 --> 00:18:42,831
They put him in tribulations, and he left Islam.

225
00:18:46,091 --> 00:18:50,785
So, the others two headed to Madina, Umar(عُمَر) and Ayaash(عياش).

226
00:18:51,888 --> 00:18:54,838
They reached to Quba'a(القُباء) or Qiba'a(قِبَاء), both are correct,

227
00:18:57,147 --> 00:19:01,666
which is outside Madina and they were hosted there.

228
00:19:03,917 --> 00:19:07,766
But Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) being a dedicated man, that he was and the hard worker

229
00:19:08,233 --> 00:19:17,201
and the one, who put his life on the line and his effort, his wealth, his time to fight against the religion of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ.

230
00:19:17,512 --> 00:19:21,008
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) wouldn't give up easily.

231
00:19:21,822 --> 00:19:31,211
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) along with his brother, Al-Haris Bin Hisham(الحارث بن هشام), they go to the Madina

232
00:19:33,245 --> 00:19:39,553
because Ayaash Ibn Abi Rabi’a(عيَّاش اِبن ابي ربيعه) was their cousin and their maternal brother.

233
00:19:40,797 --> 00:19:50,866
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) and his brother, Al-Haris(الحارث) go to meet with Ayaash(عياش), who's their cousin and maternal brother.

234
00:19:52,230 --> 00:19:54,132
Now Ayaash(عياش) was the one, who was accompanying Umar(عُمَر).

235
00:19:54,932 --> 00:20:01,058
So, they go to the Madina and Rasool Allah ﷺ did not made Hijrah(هجرة) yet, Rasool Ullah was the last ﷺ.

236
00:20:02,842 --> 00:20:05,234
So, they go to Ayaash(عياش) and they say;

237
00:20:06,175 --> 00:20:22,846
Your mother, who is also their mother, made an oath that, she will not seek shade, and she will not comb her hair, until you come back.

238
00:20:25,409 --> 00:20:33,651
 His mother was a Mushrik(مشرك) and she made an oath that she will going to stand in the sun of Makkah and she is not gonna comb her hair.

239
00:20:33,955 --> 00:20:35,993
So you see that, that’s a difficult oath!

240
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:41,413
The Sun of Makkah, and not combing your hair, very difficult thing.

241
00:20:42,719 --> 00:20:43,583
فَرَّقَّ لَهَا

242
00:20:43,745 --> 00:20:47,221
Umar(عُمَر) is narrating the story and he said: So, Ayaash(عياش) felt sorry for his mother.

243
00:20:48,194 --> 00:20:53,847
So, I told him: Do not believe these two liars, they want to deceive you

244
00:20:54,454 --> 00:20:56,105
and do not worry about your mother,

245
00:20:56,529 --> 00:21:00,357
because when the heat of Makkah picks up, she is going to seek shade

246
00:21:00,781 --> 00:21:03,952
and when her head gets full of lice, she is going to comb it.

247
00:21:07,458 --> 00:21:09,673
Emotions cannot fool Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

248
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:12,798
He cannot be tricked, he said:

249
00:21:12,822 --> 00:21:14,924
لَسْتُ بِالْخِبْ وَلَاالخِبْ يَخْدَعْنِي

250
00:21:15,513 --> 00:21:18,662
I am not a deceiver, but in the same time, no one can deceive me.

251
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:22,419
Umar(عُمَر) suspected that these men were lying.

252
00:21:22,911 --> 00:21:29,813
So, he said: Do not worry about it, and this oath that your mother made, she would not be able to carry on with it.

253
00:21:31,150 --> 00:21:34,166
Lice will fill up her hair and she will have to comb it, eventually.

254
00:21:36,766 --> 00:21:43,015
Ayaash(عياش) he said:

255
00:21:43,521 --> 00:21:50,273
No! I have to go and fulfill the oath of my mother and I also have some money there, that I want to get,

256
00:21:50,653 --> 00:21:54,027
I have some money that I want to get from Makkah.

257
00:21:55,139 --> 00:21:56,435
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him:

258
00:21:57,188 --> 00:22:01,780
You know that, I am one of the wealthy men of Makkah,

259
00:22:03,358 --> 00:22:06,987
I will give you half of my wealth but don't go!

260
00:22:09,347 --> 00:22:11,147
Ayaash(عياش) said: No! I must go.

261
00:22:13,253 --> 00:22:14,590
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن ألخطاب) said:

262
00:22:14,630 --> 00:22:21,827
 Well if you insist, this camel of mine is strong, obedient and fast, take it

263
00:22:22,662 --> 00:22:27,690
 and you ever see anything suspicious you can run away on its back.

264
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:33,693
And he gave him his camel, so they left Madina.

265
00:22:35,109 --> 00:22:38,158
After a while, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) told Ayaash(عياش),

266
00:22:39,210 --> 00:22:42,161
O my brother! This camel of mine is horrible,

267
00:22:43,229 --> 00:22:46,437
do you never mind, if we both share your camel?

268
00:22:47,107 --> 00:22:50,101
Ayaash(عياش) being the naive man he is, said: Yes, yes, of course.

269
00:22:51,378 --> 00:22:58,236
As soon as the camels sat down Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) and Al-Haris(الحارث) attacked Ayaash(عياش),

270
00:22:58,653 --> 00:23:01,606
 they tied him up and dragged him back to Makkah.

271
00:23:02,673 --> 00:23:09,328
And they put him under the Trials, the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) and he also gave up Islam.

272
00:23:15,546 --> 00:23:22,079
Umar(عُمَر) said: We used to consider and they used to also consider that whoever, gives up Islam

273
00:23:22,151 --> 00:23:25,984
after they know Allahعَزّ وجَلّ there is no repentance for them.

274
00:23:26,108 --> 00:23:28,526
That’s it! They have no hope whatsoever.

275
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:35,130
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Madina we asked him about the situation of these men.

276
00:23:36,050 --> 00:23:44,240
So Allahعَزّ وجَلّ revealed the Ayaat(آيات) in Surat az-Zumar(سورة الزمر) Verses 52 to 55.

277
00:23:45,531 --> 00:23:49,839
قُلْ يعِبَادِىَ الَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُواْ عَلَى أَنفُسِهِمْ لاَ تَقْنَطُواْ مِن رَّحْمَةِ اللَّهِ

278
00:23:50,708 --> 00:23:54,882
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعاً إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ َ۞

279
00:23:56,280 --> 00:24:01,971
وَأَنِـيبُواْ إِلَى رَبِّكُمْ وَأَسْلِمُواْ لَهُ مِن قَبْلِ أَن يَأْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ ثُمَّ لاَ تُنصَرُونَ َ۞

280
00:24:02,635 --> 00:24:09,278
وَاتَّبِعُـواْ أَحْسَنَ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكُم مِّن رَّبِّكُـمْ مِّن قَبْلِ أَن يَأْتِيَكُـمُ الْعَذَابُ بَغْتَةً وَأَنتُمْ لاَ تَشْعُرُونَ۞

281
00:24:10,635 --> 00:24:15,346
Say, O My servants, who have transgressed against their souls!

282
00:24:15,711 --> 00:24:21,310
Despair not of the mercy of Allah, For Allah forgives all sins.

283
00:24:21,814 --> 00:24:24,354
For He is Oft-Forgiving, and Merciful.

284
00:24:25,335 --> 00:24:28,652
And turn to your Lord in repentance and bow to His will

285
00:24:29,208 --> 00:24:34,301
before the penalty comes on you, after that, you shall not be helped.

286
00:24:35,800 --> 00:24:39,460
And follow the best of that of what has been revealed to you from your Lord

287
00:24:39,866 --> 00:24:44,814
before the penalty comes on you, of a sudden, while you perceive not.

288
00:24:46,644 --> 00:24:51,330
Umar(عمر) said: As soon those Ayaat(آيات) were revealed, I wrote them down

289
00:24:51,378 --> 00:24:54,771
 and by the way, Umar(عمر) was one of few men of Quraish(قريش), who was literate

290
00:24:56,013 --> 00:25:00,471
 and the one, who taught him was the father of Abu Sufian(ابوسفيان).

291
00:25:02,491 --> 00:25:11,933
So Umar(عمر) combined many skills, physical strength, intellectual power, he was literate man,

292
00:25:12,397 --> 00:25:17,758
- he was well versed in poetry, he had a very sharp mind.

293
00:25:19,346 --> 00:25:21,344
Anyways, he writes down these verses,

294
00:25:22,420 --> 00:25:26,808
and he sends them to Makkah to Hisham Ibn Al-Haris(هشام بن الحارث),

295
00:25:27,296 --> 00:25:30,130
One of the man, who stayed behind and gave up Islam.

296
00:25:30,761 --> 00:25:32,731
All what Umar(عمر) did was, write down these verses.

297
00:25:33,739 --> 00:25:40,789
Hisham(هشام) said: I received this scroll and I would go to the valleys, and mountains and read the verse

298
00:25:41,261 --> 00:25:44,892
and I would read it again and again and I did not understand what Umar(عمر) meant.

299
00:25:46,118 --> 00:25:50,589
I didn't understand the meaning of these verses, because Umar(عمر) did not write any commentary.

300
00:25:51,020 --> 00:25:56,346
The Ayaat(آيات) say that Allah is forgiving, and if you have committed wrong, against yourself, Allah will Forgive you.

301
00:25:59,344 --> 00:26:05,193
So, Al-Hisham(الهشام) said: I asked Allahعزُّوَجل and I prayed to Allah to give me the understanding.

302
00:26:05,783 --> 00:26:08,502
So dear brothers and sisters, when you do not understand something, pray to Allah.

303
00:26:09,133 --> 00:26:10,601
You know Ibn Taymiah(ابن تيميه) used to say,

304
00:26:11,244 --> 00:26:16,808
that I would recite a verse and I would go and read the tafseer(تفسير) of the Ayah(آية),

305
00:26:16,883 --> 00:26:23,332
 and I would read eighty different views on this particular verse but none of them would appeal to me,

306
00:26:24,228 --> 00:26:31,818
so I would go out to the ruins and I would stick my face in the dirt and make Sujood(سجود)

307
00:26:32,411 --> 00:26:35,525
and pray to Allahعزُّوَجل to give me the understanding

308
00:26:37,064 --> 00:26:39,169
and this is the scholar Ibn Taymiah(ابن تيميه).

309
00:26:40,264 --> 00:26:43,643
So, Hisham Bin Haris(هشام بن حارث) was praying to Allah to give him the understanding.

310
00:26:44,607 --> 00:26:53,095
He said: Then I realized that these verses were revealed talking about us and the ones, who are in similar situations.

311
00:26:54,020 --> 00:26:57,843
 And I realized that Allahعزُّوَجل is giving us another chance.

312
00:26:59,962 --> 00:27:04,413
And that's when, I mounted my camel and went towards Madina.

313
00:27:11,899 --> 00:27:19,346
Brothers and sisters, there is very important lesson to learn here from this story of Hijrah(هجرة) of Umar(عمر) and Ayaash(عياش).

314
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:22,838
Umar(عمر) told Ayaash(عياش), don't believe them, they want to deceive you.

315
00:27:25,549 --> 00:27:27,544
The important lesson to learn here is:

316
00:27:27,616 --> 00:27:30,306
Never Ever Trust Al-Kuffar(الكفار).

317
00:27:31,936 --> 00:27:33,545
Do Not Trust Them

318
00:27:36,817 --> 00:27:40,831
You might argue and say but my neighbor is such a nice person

319
00:27:42,347 --> 00:27:49,255
My classmates are very nice, my co-workers, they are just fabulous people, they are so decent, and honest.

320
00:27:50,950 --> 00:27:55,481
You know the only problem is that we Muslims are giving Islam a bad name,

321
00:27:57,551 --> 00:27:59,981
if these terrorists would just stop, what they are doing?

322
00:28:00,291 --> 00:28:03,748
And we give them Dawah(دعوة) in the right way, everybody is gonna become Muslim.

323
00:28:08,370 --> 00:28:12,528
Now, I am not going to argue that your neighbor is not nice person or your classmate

324
00:28:12,917 --> 00:28:16,990
they're very well, they truly might be decent and nice people.

325
00:28:20,117 --> 00:28:26,839
But brothers, when you make a judgment about Kuffr(كفر) you do not Make a judgment based on your neighbor

326
00:28:26,879 --> 00:28:30,149
 and then you make a Qiyas(قياس) alright, and then you generalize

327
00:28:31,436 --> 00:28:34,771
and you make a judgment according to one person, that you know.

328
00:28:36,191 --> 00:28:39,343
Because this person that you know is not the one, calling the shots.

329
00:28:40,574 --> 00:28:44,371
And when Qur’an talks about Kuffar(كفار) it talks about the leaders of Kuffr(كفر).

330
00:28:44,947 --> 00:28:46,652
The ones, who are pulling the strings.

331
00:28:48,104 --> 00:28:53,310
Do not make a judgment on Kuffr(كفر) based on Jane Bow and John doe.

332
00:28:53,642 --> 00:28:56,960
You don't, make it base on, Joe six pack or sally soccer-mom.

333
00:28:57,599 --> 00:29:00,439
You make the judgment based on the leaders of the Al-Kuffr(الكفر).

334
00:29:01,206 --> 00:29:04,465
