508
00:41:26,626 --> 00:41:31,888
وَآيَةُ الْحِجَابِ، قُلْتُ: يا رسول الله، لَوْ أَمَرْتَ نِسَاءَكَ أَنْ يَحْتَجِبْنَ

509
00:41:32,217 --> 00:41:36,775
فَإِنَه’ يُكَلِّمُهُنَّ اَلْبَرُّ وَالْفَاجِرْ، فَنَزَلَتْ آيَةَ الْحِجَابْ،

510
00:41:37,729 --> 00:41:43,372
I told Rasool Allah ﷺ, O Rasool Ullah, why don’t you order your women to have Hijaab(حجاب)?

511
00:41:43,701 --> 00:41:49,121
Because, they are speaking to men who could be good or evil.

512
00:41:49,569 --> 00:41:52,378
And that’s when the Ayah(آية) of Hijaab(حجاب) was revealed.

513
00:41:54,654 --> 00:42:00,342
وَاجْتَمَعَ نِسَاءُ النَّبِي صلى الله عليه وسلم فِيْ الْغِيْرَةْ عَلِيْهِ

514
00:42:00,876 --> 00:42:07,902
فَقُلْتُ لَهُنَّ: عَسَى رَبُّه’ إِنْ طَلَّقَكُنَّ، أَنْ يُبْدِلَه’أَزْوَاجَا خَيْرَا مِّنْكُنْ، فَانَزَلَتِ هَذِهِ الّآيَةْ

515
00:42:08,474 --> 00:42:11,070
The wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ had jealousy

516
00:42:12,419 --> 00:42:16,337
and the wives of Rasool Allahﷺ, some of them,

517
00:42:16,669 --> 00:42:25,203
because of their jealousy they made this plan and they told Rasool Allah ﷺ something,

518
00:42:25,522 --> 00:42:28,282
 the whole thing was because of their jealousy between them.

519
00:42:29,959 --> 00:42:34,277
Umar(عُمَر) caught word of that, so he went to the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ he brought them together

520
00:42:34,953 --> 00:42:40,647
and he said: If you don’t stop what you are doing?

521
00:42:41,948 --> 00:42:46,000
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will replace you with better wives for His Messenger,

522
00:42:47,216 --> 00:42:49,256
and he was giving them this harsh advice.

523
00:42:49,886 --> 00:42:53,394
So, one of these wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ was upset and she said;

524
00:42:54,240 --> 00:42:55,057
What do you think?

525
00:42:55,286 --> 00:42:59,611
Rasool Allah ﷺ is unable to give us Naseeha(نصيحة), so that you come and give us Naseeha(نصيحة).

526
00:42:59,904 --> 00:43:01,466
Who are you to come and give us Naseeha(نصيحة)?

527
00:43:01,506 --> 00:43:03,031
Rasool Allah ﷺ could do that.

528
00:43:03,865 --> 00:43:06,590
But an Ayah(آية) was revealed saying,

529
00:43:07,892 --> 00:43:13,071
عَسَىٰ رَبُّهُ إِنْ طَلَّقَكُنَّ أَنْ يُبْدِلَهُ أَزْوَاجًا خَيْرًا مِنْكُنَّ مُسْلِمَاتٍ

530
00:43:13,140 --> 00:43:18,260
مُؤْمِنَاتٍ قَانِتَاتٍ تَائِبَاتٍ عَابِدَاتٍ سَائِحَاتٍ ثَيِّبَاتٍ وَأَبْكَارًا۞

531
00:43:19,293 --> 00:43:27,013
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ can give him, wives better than you to the end of the Ayah(آية),

532
00:43:28,652 --> 00:43:32,933
These are three event which he mentions that’s not it, but there are some other events that happened.

533
00:43:34,304 --> 00:43:40,576
Abdullah Ibn Obeye(عبدالله ابن ابئ), the leader of the Munafiqeen(منافقين), he was the top Munafiq(منافق) in the Madina.

534
00:43:41,961 --> 00:43:51,004
When he passed away Rasool Allahﷺ wanted to lead his Janazah(جنازة) after all, what he has done.

535
00:43:51,745 --> 00:43:54,373
Rasool Allah ﷺ still wanted to lead his Janazah(جنازة).

536
00:43:55,203 --> 00:43:58,744
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is standing ready to start his Salah(صلاة).

537
00:43:58,931 --> 00:44:01,727
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) comes and stands in front of him,

538
00:44:03,602 --> 00:44:05,135
and he says; O Messenger of Allah

539
00:44:05,739 --> 00:44:09,350
You want to pray on this man, who did this and this and this and this...

540
00:44:10,174 --> 00:44:14,409
He said: When I kept on going Rasool Allah ﷺ was only smiling.

541
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:19,569
When I was not stopping and I was mentioning all his evil sins,

542
00:44:19,771 --> 00:44:22,642
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Move away from me, Umar(عُمَر).

543
00:44:23,603 --> 00:44:25,293
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ had told me:

544
00:44:25,603 --> 00:44:32,409
اسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ أَوْ لَا تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ إِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِينَ مَرَّةً فَلَنْ يَغْفِرَ اللَّهُ لَهُمْ

545
00:44:35,484 --> 00:44:39,789
Ask for forgiveness, for them or don’t ask for forgiveness for them

546
00:44:40,404 --> 00:44:44,354
even, if you ask Forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will not forgive them.

547
00:44:45,261 --> 00:44:49,188
So, if I know that if I make Istighfaar(استغفار) seventy one times,

548
00:44:49,576 --> 00:44:52,783
if I know that would help them, I would do so.

549
00:44:58,242 --> 00:45:01,127
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ prayed on Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن أبيئ).

550
00:45:01,517 --> 00:45:06,931
And then he followed his Janazah(جنازة) and stood on his grave, asking Allah to forgive him.

551
00:45:08,051 --> 00:45:14,126
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ was surprised by my boldness.

552
00:45:14,634 --> 00:45:18,349
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) comes and stands infront of Rasool Allah ﷺ preventing him from, leading the Salah(صلاة).

553
00:45:19,689 --> 00:45:24,404
And he argues with Rasool Allah ﷺ, until Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; Move away.

554
00:45:27,017 --> 00:45:31,742
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) says; A short while after that Allahعَزّ وجَلّ reveals the Ayah(آية),

555
00:45:32,062 --> 00:45:36,151
وَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلَىٰ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ مَاتَ أَبَدًا وَلَا تَقُمْ عَلَىٰ قَبْرِهِ ۖ

556
00:45:36,390 --> 00:45:39,478
إِنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَمَاتُوا وَهُمْ فَاسِقُونَ۞

557
00:45:40,402 --> 00:45:41,832
At-Tauba(ألتوبة) Verse 84.

558
00:45:42,596 --> 00:45:51,292
Allah says; Do not ever pray for any of them, that dies and do not stand on his grave

559
00:45:51,748 --> 00:45:56,036
for they rejected Allah and His Messenger and they died as non believers.

560
00:45:57,033 --> 00:46:00,475
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ is telling Muhammadﷺ never ever pray on them again.

561
00:46:01,558 --> 00:46:03,689
So, it came to confirm what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said.

562
00:46:05,509 --> 00:46:09,844
In the Battle of Badr(بدر) Rasool Allah ﷺ have seventy prisoners of war.

563
00:46:10,641 --> 00:46:15,479
This is first battle of Islam, so there were many new things

564
00:46:16,063 --> 00:46:20,257
and the Laws weren’t revealed yet, relating to those issues.

565
00:46:20,368 --> 00:46:23,105
One of them was the issue of Prisoners of War.

566
00:46:24,276 --> 00:46:25,874
They have seventy prisoners of war.

567
00:46:26,090 --> 00:46:27,168
What should we do with them?

568
00:46:27,755 --> 00:46:30,474
As usual Rasool Allah ﷺ makes Shoora(شورى).

569
00:46:31,472 --> 00:46:33,904
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

570
00:46:35,095 --> 00:46:45,037
These are our relatives, our fathers, brothers, cousins, why don’t we ransom them?

571
00:46:46,946 --> 00:46:50,194
The money that is paid is gonna strengthen the Muslims

572
00:46:50,980 --> 00:46:54,180
and these men might grow one day, to become Muslim

573
00:46:55,661 --> 00:46:57,154
and that would strengthen Islam.

574
00:47:00,610 --> 00:47:02,743
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: O Messenger of Allah!

575
00:47:03,097 --> 00:47:04,997
I disagree with what Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said.

576
00:47:07,109 --> 00:47:13,730
I say that you should hand over to Ali(علي) his brother Aqeel(عقيل) to execute him.

577
00:47:14,579 --> 00:47:19,176
You hand over to Hamza(حمزه) his brother so and so to execute him,

578
00:47:19,508 --> 00:47:22,311
you hand over to me my relative to execute him,

579
00:47:22,458 --> 00:47:23,486
and he went on and on.

580
00:47:23,766 --> 00:47:27,659
So, Allah knows the we have no mercy in our hearts for the disbeliever.

581
00:47:29,031 --> 00:47:32,489
حَتَى يَرَى الله اِنَّه’ لَيْسَ فِيْ قُلُوْبِنَا هَوَادَةْ عَلَى الْكُفَّارْ

582
00:47:33,120 --> 00:47:36,055
To give a message to the believers and to disbelievers

583
00:47:36,311 --> 00:47:40,391
and to show Allah that we have no mercy in our hearts for Kuffr(كفر).

584
00:47:43,259 --> 00:47:47,667
Abdullah Ibn Rawaha(عبدالله ابن رواحة) said: My view is that you dig a ditch for them, a trench

585
00:47:48,282 --> 00:47:50,310
and you fill it with wood and you burn them.

586
00:47:50,879 --> 00:47:52,937
That was the opinion of Abdullah Ibn Rawaha(عبدالله ابن رواحة).

587
00:47:53,821 --> 00:47:59,751
Rasool Allah ﷺ left and the Sahabah(صحابه) were debating which opinion would he choose

588
00:47:59,984 --> 00:48:02,457
some say Abdullah Ibn Rawaha(عبدالله ابن رواحة) some say Umar(عُمَر) and some say Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

589
00:48:03,517 --> 00:48:12,830
Rasool Allah ﷺ comes out and he adopts the opinion of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), that we accept ransom.

590
00:48:16,682 --> 00:48:23,479
And there is a longer Hadith(حديث) in Al-Ahmad(الاحمد) relating to this.

591
00:48:27,071 --> 00:48:28,654
Rasool Allah ﷺ came out and he said:

592
00:48:30,237 --> 00:48:36,041
إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَيُلِينُ قُلُوبَ رِجَالٍ فِيهِ ، حَتَّى تَكُونَ أَلْيَنَ مِنَ اللَّبَنِ

593
00:48:36,574 --> 00:48:43,834
وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَيَشُدُّ قُلُوبَ رِجَالٍ فِيهِ ، حَتَّى تَكُونَ أَشَدَّ مِنَ الْحِجَارَةِ

594
00:48:44,459 --> 00:48:50,533
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ softens some hearts so they become as soft as milk

595
00:48:51,187 --> 00:48:56,041
and Allahعَزّ وجَلّ makes some heart hard and strong so that they become like rocks.

596
00:48:57,311 --> 00:49:03,857
وَإِنَّ مَثَلَكَ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ كَمَثَلِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَام

597
00:49:04,341 --> 00:49:08,927
قَالَ : فَمَنْ تَبِعَنِي فَإِنَّهُ مِنِّي ، وَمَنْ عَصَانِي فَإِنَّكَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ۞

598
00:49:09,549 --> 00:49:15,489
And the analogy of you, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is like Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) you are similar to Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), who said:

599
00:49:15,765 --> 00:49:21,464
Whoever follows me is from me, and whoever disobeys me, You are Forgiving and Merciful.

600
00:49:22,221 --> 00:49:23,883
And you are also similar to 'Eesa(عيسى).

601
00:49:24,173 --> 00:49:29,711
قالَ: إِنْ تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ ۖ وَإِنْ تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَإِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ۞

602
00:49:31,261 --> 00:49:36,399
If You punish them they are Your servants and if Your Forgive them; You are Al-Aziz ul Hakeem(العزيزالحكيم)

603
00:49:37,327 --> 00:49:39,511
وَاِنَّ مَثَلَكَ يا عمر كَمَثَلِ نُوْحْ

604
00:49:40,102 --> 00:49:41,880
You Umar(عُمَر) are similar to Noah(نوح).

605
00:49:42,471 --> 00:49:45,740
وَقَالَ نُوحٌ رَبِّ لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ دَيَّارًا۞

606
00:49:46,133 --> 00:49:50,191
Noah(نوح) said: O Allah do not leave any disbeliever on the face of the earth.

607
00:49:51,179 --> 00:49:53,776
And you are also similar to Musa(موسى), who said:

608
00:49:54,742 --> 00:50:00,621
رَبَّنَا اطْمِسْ عَلَىٰ أَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاشْدُدْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوا حَتَّىٰ يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْأَلِيمَ۞

609
00:50:01,010 --> 00:50:07,313
O Allah make their hearts sealed so that they do not believe until they see the punishment.

610
00:50:09,163 --> 00:50:14,381
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted, the advice of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

611
00:50:19,056 --> 00:50:27,840
Later on, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه see's Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) crying.

612
00:50:29,152 --> 00:50:31,671
So, he goes to them and says: Why are you crying?

613
00:50:32,673 --> 00:50:36,471
If it makes me cry, then I will cry otherwise, I will force myself to cry.

614
00:50:37,309 --> 00:50:47,990
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We are crying because Allahعَزّوجَلّ, presented, me with the punishment that was going to befall us

615
00:50:48,244 --> 00:50:49,906
 because we accepted the ransom.

616
00:50:51,261 --> 00:50:53,745
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed to me the following verses.

617
00:50:54,677 --> 00:50:58,571
مَا كَانَ لِنَبِيٍّ أَنْ يَكُونَ لَهُ أَسْرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ يُثْخِنَ فِي الْأَرْضِ

618
00:50:59,336 --> 00:51:04,075
تُرِيدُونَ عَرَضَ الدُّنْيَا وَاللَّهُ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۞

619
00:51:04,457 --> 00:51:09,135
لَوْلَا كِتَابٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيم۞

620
00:51:09,448 --> 00:51:11,797
Al-Anfaal(ألأنفال) Verse 67-68.

621
00:51:12,898 --> 00:51:19,055
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: It is not fitting for a prophet that he should have prisoners of war,

622
00:51:19,233 --> 00:51:22,472
until he has caused bloodshed among the disbelievers.

623
00:51:23,160 --> 00:51:25,743
You look for temporal goods of this world

624
00:51:25,960 --> 00:51:30,168
but Allah looks at the hereafter and Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.

625
00:51:30,859 --> 00:51:33,812
Had it not been for previously ordainment from Allah

626
00:51:34,622 --> 00:51:38,342
a severe punishment would have reached you for the ransom that you took.

627
00:51:38,366 --> 00:51:42,363
So, Allahعَزّ وجَلّ is telling Muhammadﷺ this was the first time, that you fight with the Kuffar(كفار),

628
00:51:42,641 --> 00:51:44,003
you should have executed them all.

629
00:51:44,627 --> 00:51:48,572
You should have caused bloodshed on the land, among the Kuffar(كفار).

630
00:51:49,278 --> 00:51:52,963
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ disapproved, taking the ransom.

631
00:51:54,006 --> 00:51:56,524
But Allah says that punishment was gonna come down

632
00:51:56,892 --> 00:51:58,992
however, it was already ordained.

633
00:51:59,381 --> 00:52:01,500
That the Ghaneema(غنيمة) is Halal(حلال) for this Ummah(امة).

634
00:52:01,655 --> 00:52:03,633
So, that’s why the punishment was with held.

635
00:52:04,110 --> 00:52:10,150
So Qur’an came approving the opinion of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه when it came to those prisoners of war.

636
00:52:11,645 --> 00:52:12,434
ANOTHER INCIDENT:

637
00:52:12,851 --> 00:52:22,092
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent a servant to call Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and this was at noon.

638
00:52:24,029 --> 00:52:29,243
In those days, they didn’t have, any locked gates, doors.

639
00:52:29,652 --> 00:52:36,975
All what they had was mud houses very small.

640
00:52:37,514 --> 00:52:44,812
And there would be a curtain hanging on the entrance and you just walk in.

641
00:52:46,740 --> 00:52:50,478
So, Umar(عُمَر) was sleeping and part of his body was uncovered.

642
00:52:51,220 --> 00:52:55,441
So, this servant comes in and he calls Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

643
00:52:55,770 --> 00:53:06,385
Umar(عُمَر) said: O Allah! Ban allowing people to visit us, at these times.

644
00:53:07,667 --> 00:53:11,834
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) felt uncomfortable for this man just walking in,

645
00:53:12,330 --> 00:53:15,097
and seeing him with part of his body uncovered.

646
00:53:16,749 --> 00:53:20,927
Now, there is already an Ayah(آية) that was revealed of Istezaan(إستئذان)

647
00:53:21,884 --> 00:53:24,359
that, you should seek permission before you go in.

648
00:53:24,835 --> 00:53:27,549
However, this was for foreign people.

649
00:53:28,323 --> 00:53:38,721
But with your slaves and your children and your direct family members, there wasn’t any permission, they just walk in at any time.

650
00:53:39,757 --> 00:53:42,493
So, this was the servant of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and he walked in.

651
00:53:43,739 --> 00:53:45,963
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية),

652
00:53:46,396 --> 00:53:53,084
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لِيَسْتَأْذِنْكُمُ الَّذِينَ مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ وَالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَبْلُغُوا الْحُلُمَ مِنْكُمْ ثَلَاثَ مَرَّاتٍ

653
00:53:53,985 --> 00:54:01,052
مِنْ قَبْلِ صَلَاةِ الْفَجْرِ وَحِينَ تَضَعُونَ ثِيَابَكُمْ مِنَ الظَّهِيرَةِ وَمِنْ بَعْدِ صَلَاةِ الْعِشَاءِ

654
00:54:01,433 --> 00:54:02,713
ثَلَاثُ عَوْرَاتٍ لَكُمْ

655
00:54:03,090 --> 00:54:05,319
This is Surah Nur(سورة النور) Verse 57-58.

656
00:54:06,155 --> 00:54:12,577
O you who believe! Let those whom your right hands possesses and the children among you,

657
00:54:12,916 --> 00:54:16,063
who have not come up age, ask not your permission

658
00:54:16,415 --> 00:54:19,707
before they come to your presence on three occasions,

659
00:54:20,245 --> 00:54:26,917
before morning prayers, while you undress for the noon day heat, and after the Esha(عشاء) prayer.

660
00:54:27,142 --> 00:54:29,789
These are your three times of undress.

661
00:54:30,722 --> 00:54:36,158
So, your children who are not over the age of puberty yet,

662
00:54:37,455 --> 00:54:41,262
need to ask permission before they come into the room.

663
00:54:41,842 --> 00:54:44,902
At these different three times, after Salaat-Al-Esha(صلاة العشآء)

664
00:54:46,178 --> 00:54:48,020
and before Salat-Al-Fajr(صلاة الفجر)

665
00:54:48,636 --> 00:54:51,303
and after Salat-Al-Zuhar(صلاة الظهر).

666
00:54:51,732 --> 00:55:00,405
The Siasta time because in the hot climate of Madina, they would sleep at mid-day.

667
00:55:01,833 --> 00:55:07,400
And Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says this is one of the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur’an that people are not practicing anymore.

668
00:55:08,380 --> 00:55:11,858
He was saying about those old days, and now it's not practiced.

669
00:55:11,979 --> 00:55:17,358
You need to teach your children this habit that they don’t just walk into your room at any time.

670
00:55:17,397 --> 00:55:21,184
 They can walk in at any other time but these three times they shouldn’t.

671
00:55:21,280 --> 00:55:23,874
 They should seek permission first.

672
00:55:31,207 --> 00:55:38,319
We'll move to the next section which is the:

673
00:55:38,390 --> 00:55:43,162
JIHAD(جهاد) OF UMAR(عُمَر) WITH RASOOL ALLAH ﷺ:

674
00:55:43,719 --> 00:55:47,747
We already mentioned part of story of Badr(بدر) the prisoners of war,

675
00:55:48,112 --> 00:55:52,457
there are two other incidences that happened in Ghazwat Badr(غزوة البدر),

676
00:55:54,362 --> 00:55:56,760
 You have Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو).

677
00:55:56,895 --> 00:56:02,174
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو) was very eloquent speaker from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

678
00:56:03,106 --> 00:56:06,995
And he used his, this ability to fight Islam.

679
00:56:08,233 --> 00:56:10,106
 He was one of the Prisoner Of War.

680
00:56:12,074 --> 00:56:17,219
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

681
00:56:17,259 --> 00:56:23,636
O Rasool Ullah, Allow me to pluck out the front teeth of Suhail(سهيل)

682
00:56:24,373 --> 00:56:30,352
so that his tongue would hang out and he wouldn’t be able to speak against you again.

683
00:56:31,945 --> 00:56:35,153
Take out the front teeth, so that his tongue would just come out of his mouth

684
00:56:35,758 --> 00:56:39,068
 and he would not be able to talk against you again.

685
00:56:39,440 --> 00:56:40,608
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

686
00:56:41,723 --> 00:56:50,260
لَا أُمَثِّلُ بِه فَيُمَثِّلُ الله بِيْ وَإِنْ كُنْتُ نَبِيَّا، وَعَسَى أَنْ يَقُوْمَ مَقَامًا لَا تَذُمُّه

687
00:56:51,139 --> 00:56:58,259
He said: I am not gonna mutilate him, because Allah will mutilate me, even if I am a Prophet.

688
00:56:59,382 --> 00:57:04,149
And maybe one day he will take a stand that will impress you.

689
00:57:06,342 --> 00:57:14,241
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said, that I am not allowed to do something like that and then he said:

690
00:57:14,964 --> 00:57:21,478
And one day he will take a stance that, you will like.

691
00:57:22,792 --> 00:57:23,498
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

692
00:57:23,681 --> 00:57:31,299
this disbeliever, Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو), who became Muslim very late, after Sulh-Al-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

693
00:57:32,046 --> 00:57:38,101
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, the people of Makkah, many of them commited Ridda(ردة)

694
00:57:39,764 --> 00:57:45,678
and the governor of Makkah Attab Ibn Usaid(عتاب ابن اسيد), who was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

695
00:57:47,349 --> 00:57:48,965
he went into hiding.

696
00:57:49,922 --> 00:57:55,793
It was Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو), who stood up and invited the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and said:

697
00:57:56,117 --> 00:57:59,735
The death of Muhammadﷺ, would  only make Islam stronger

698
00:58:00,307 --> 00:58:03,499
and whoever gives up Islam, I am going to behead him.

699
00:58:04,068 --> 00:58:07,973
And it was only because of Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو), that the people of Makkah remained on Islam.

700
00:58:08,890 --> 00:58:11,766
That was the position that Rasool Allah ﷺ was referring to.

701
00:58:12,926 --> 00:58:19,694
So, don’t be in a hurry don’t punish this man, because one day this tongue will benefit Islam.

702
00:58:22,511 --> 00:58:26,609
Another occasion, was Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير ابن وهب),

703
00:58:26,733 --> 00:58:30,653
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير ابن وهب) his son was taken as a Prisoner of War.

704
00:58:30,910 --> 00:58:32,865
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير ابن وهب) was a very wicked man.

705
00:58:34,972 --> 00:58:40,253
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير ابن وهب) after the Battle of Badr(بدر), he went to Madina.

706
00:58:42,783 --> 00:58:47,800
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was sitting up with some of the Sahabah(صحابه), talking about the Battle of Badr(بدر).

707
00:58:55,015 --> 00:59:03,389
And he saw Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير ابن وهب) approaching, with his sword hanging from his neck.

708
00:59:05,125 --> 00:59:06,795
Umar(عُمَر) said: That dog,

709
00:59:07,375 --> 00:59:08,931
هذا كلب عدوالله

710
00:59:09,367 --> 00:59:13,201
Is the enemy of Allah and he is here for evil.

711
00:59:13,943 --> 00:59:15,403
You can see the Farasah(فراسه) of Umar(عُمَر),

712
00:59:17,792 --> 00:59:19,387
 he said: This man came for evil.

713
00:59:20,873 --> 00:59:24,191
And he immediately, rushed to Rasool Allah ﷺ, he came and said:

714
00:59:24,481 --> 00:59:27,743
The enemy of Allah Umair(عمير) is here and he is upto no good.

715
00:59:31,385 --> 00:59:33,212
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Bring him in!

716
00:59:33,252 --> 00:59:38,278
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) goes and he wraps the sword around Umair(عمير) and he ties him up

717
00:59:39,021 --> 00:59:40,963
and he brings him in to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

718
00:59:41,003 --> 00:59:41,812
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

719
00:59:41,883 --> 00:59:42,745
أَرْسِله يا عمر

720
00:59:43,027 --> 00:59:43,943
Leave him alone.

721
00:59:45,831 --> 00:59:47,196
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ tells Umair(عمير),

722
00:59:47,217 --> 00:59:47,756
مَا جَـاءَبِكُمْ

723
00:59:47,862 --> 00:59:48,669
Why did you come?

724
00:59:49,259 --> 00:59:52,939
He said: O Muhammad(محمد),

725
00:59:53,972 --> 00:59:55,662
First thing that he actually said was,

726
00:59:56,151 --> 00:59:57,053
اَنْعِمْ صَبَاحًا

727
00:59:57,216 --> 00:59:58,058
Good Morning.

728
00:59:59,606 --> 01:00:03,606
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We have a better greeting then that.

729
01:00:03,976 --> 01:00:05,460
السلام و عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

730
01:00:05,484 --> 01:00:07,728
Allah has given us something better than good night and good morning.

731
01:00:11,129 --> 01:00:12,331
مَا جَاءَبِكَ يا عمير

732
01:00:12,621 --> 01:00:13,443
Why did you come here?

733
01:00:13,602 --> 01:00:16,030
He said: I came here to ransom my son.

734
01:00:17,579 --> 01:00:20,253
He said: Umair(عمير), tell me the truth, why did you come here?

735
01:00:20,785 --> 01:00:23,599
He said: I am telling you the truth that’s the only reason, why I came here.

736
01:00:24,937 --> 01:00:29,651
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: So, what is that sword doing on your neck?

737
01:00:30,474 --> 01:00:30,723
He said:

738
01:00:30,747 --> 01:00:33,414
قَبَّحَهَا الله مِنْ سُيُوْفِ وَهَلْ أَغْنَت عَنَّا شَيْئَا؟

739
01:00:33,805 --> 01:00:36,830
May evil befall all of these swords, what good have they done us?

740
01:00:37,544 --> 01:00:38,472
We lost in Badr(بدر).

741
01:00:39,592 --> 01:00:42,381
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No, that’s not why you came here.

742
01:00:42,988 --> 01:00:47,530
The reason why you came here, is because you have met with Sufwan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان ابن امية), next to Al-Ka’aba(ألكعبه)

743
01:00:50,083 --> 01:00:57,971
and you told Sufwan(صفوان), that if it wasn’t because you have daughters

744
01:00:58,571 --> 01:01:08,364
and you fear for their welfare, if you die and you are in debt, you would go and kill Muhammad(محمد).

745
01:01:09,780 --> 01:01:11,967
And then Sufwan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان ابن امية) told you,

746
01:01:12,301 --> 01:01:15,681
I am going to take care of your daughters just as if they were mine,

747
01:01:15,833 --> 01:01:19,968
and I am going to pay your debt and you agreed, to come and kill me.

748
01:01:20,218 --> 01:01:22,009
That’s why you came here Umair(عمير).

749
01:01:23,344 --> 01:01:24,448
Umair(عمير) said:

750
01:01:25,633 --> 01:01:30,670
That conversation was witnessed by no one but me and Safwan(صفوان).

751
01:01:32,501 --> 01:01:37,090
So, I testify and bear witness that there is no god but Allah and you are the Messenger of Allah.

752
01:01:37,558 --> 01:01:38,718
He became Muslim.

753
01:01:42,608 --> 01:01:48,014
Back in Makkah, Safwan(صفوان) was telling the people, just wait, you will just hear a very good news in few days.

754
01:01:49,856 --> 01:01:51,482
You're gonna hear some very good news.

755
01:01:52,857 --> 01:01:56,429
Umair(عمير) comes back and he tells Safwan(صفوان), that I have became Muslim.

756
01:01:56,660 --> 01:01:58,727
 it was disaster for Safwan(صفوان).

757
01:02:03,378 --> 01:02:07,913
You can also notice that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had a very good sense of security.

758
01:02:10,292 --> 01:02:14,600
Because he knew that this man is intending evil

759
01:02:15,876 --> 01:02:24,007
and when he went in and grabbed him and wrapped his sword around him and took him to Rasool Allah ﷺ

760
01:02:24,317 --> 01:02:25,851
and Rasool Ullah told him to leave him alone.

761
01:02:26,037 --> 01:02:31,586
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told some Ansaar(أنْصَار), he told them be careful from this man.

762
01:02:31,782 --> 01:02:36,049
This man is here for an evil purpose, protect Rasool Allah ﷺ from him.

763
01:02:36,893 --> 01:02:41,814
So, Umar(عُمَر) had very good sense of security, you see it, in this incident

764
01:02:41,862 --> 01:02:47,783
and you can also see it, in some other stuff that we have talked about earlier.

765
01:02:47,851 --> 01:02:51,667
For example, with ‘Ayaash(عياش), he told him to be careful from Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل),

766
01:02:52,065 --> 01:02:59,661
so he had a very good sense of security and this is a good thing to have and not to be duped.

767
01:03:02,252 --> 01:03:05,113
Tayyeb(طيب), we'll carry on In Sha Allah Ta'ala(إن شاءالله تعالى) tomorrow

768
01:03:05,571 --> 01:03:11,971
with the Jihad(جهاد) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

769
01:03:12,818 --> 01:03:16,839
If you have any questions we could go to some questions, yes.

770
01:03:18,476 --> 01:03:41,946
Question From Audience.

771
01:03:41,996 --> 01:03:47,329
No, I'm not gonna mention anything else regarding that story, But I think that the points are clear.

772
01:03:48,555 --> 01:04:13,159
Question From Audience.

773
01:04:13,615 --> 01:04:16,740
How do you relate that to the issue of trusting the Kuffar(كفار)?

774
01:04:17,229 --> 01:04:43,957
Question From Audience.

775
01:04:45,019 --> 01:04:48,882
Yani(يعني) I don't see the relationship between that and the issue of the trust of the Kuffar(كفار),

776
01:04:48,919 --> 01:04:50,220
I'm not sure, I understand the question!

777
01:04:50,542 --> 01:05:08,176
Question From Audience.

778
01:05:08,201 --> 01:05:10,614
Okay, Tayeb(طيب) I think I understand what you're relating to.

779
01:05:10,779 --> 01:05:13,394
Now, there is a difference between trust and working.

780
01:05:14,604 --> 01:05:18,012
You work with Muslim and non Muslim, you work with everyone.

781
01:05:18,968 --> 01:05:21,468
There's a difference here, you work with everyone!

782
01:05:22,467 --> 01:05:26,473
But the trust goes to the ones, who believe in Allahعَزّوجَلّ the people of tawheed(توحيد).

783
01:05:28,329 --> 01:05:32,827
And when we talk about the trust issue, and not to be deceived.

784
01:05:33,137 --> 01:05:37,262
It's also relating to Aaimma Tul Kuffr(آئمة الكفر), the leadership of Kuffr(كفر).

785
01:05:38,401 --> 01:05:44,952
But the masses are deceived and the Muslims need to wake them up.

786
01:05:47,717 --> 01:05:50,755
The Da'wah(دعوة) that was given by Nooh(نوح), the Da'wah(دعوة) that was given by Saleh(صالح),

787
01:05:50,829 --> 01:05:53,320
the Da'wah(دعوة) that was given to by Hood(هود).

788
01:05:53,394 --> 01:05:54,034
Who was it given to?

789
01:05:54,054 --> 01:05:55,173
It was given to Kuffar(كفار),

790
01:05:55,779 --> 01:06:02,855
they invited Kuffar(كفار) and they woke them up, from their state of unconsciousness.

791
01:06:04,264 --> 01:06:05,595
That is what we need to do.

792
01:06:07,010 --> 01:06:14,084
Your friends, your neighbors all of these people, they could one day become Muslim,

793
01:06:15,023 --> 01:06:18,174
if they woke up from that state of Unconsciousness.

794
01:06:19,087 --> 01:06:23,075
So definitely there's in terms of establishing institutions for the Muslims,

795
01:06:24,534 --> 01:06:28,281
work needs to be done for the Muslims, whether you're living in Muslim lands or non Muslim lands.

796
01:06:30,238 --> 01:06:33,061
But the thing is that we should not put too much trust

797
01:06:34,223 --> 01:06:38,091
on what we hear from the media, or the political leadership.

798
01:06:38,970 --> 01:06:41,182
Because the real intentions are not really shown,

799
01:06:41,567 --> 01:06:44,787
just like Abu Jahal(أبوجهل) did not show his real intentions to Ayyash(عيَّاش)

800
01:06:45,179 --> 01:06:46,886
they're not showing the real intentions today.

801
01:06:50,329 --> 01:06:53,748
The sisters, if you have any questions you can write them down.

802
01:06:54,278 --> 01:06:59,166
And we don't want to deprive the sisters from be able to ask questions.

803
01:06:59,979 --> 01:07:01,004
Yes,

804
01:07:01,237 --> 01:07:16,469
Question From Audience.

805
01:07:16,913 --> 01:07:19,970
This was only relating to first battle,

806
01:07:20,565 --> 01:07:25,097
 in the first Battle, Allah didn’t want Muhammadﷺ to take Prisoners of war

807
01:07:25,255 --> 01:07:30,742
but after that the law is that it's upto the Imam(اِمَام)

808
01:07:31,177 --> 01:07:37,000
to either free them without ransom, or ransom them or execute.

809
01:07:38,210 --> 01:07:39,712
These are up to the Imam(اِمَام).

810
01:07:41,185 --> 01:07:46,271
Sisters if you have any Questions either written or spoken, you can go ahead and ask your Question.

811
01:07:49,108 --> 01:07:50,179
What is that again?

812
01:07:50,622 --> 01:07:55,532
Question From Audience.

813
01:07:55,557 --> 01:07:57,539
The Ayah(آية) doesn’t tell us, what happened to them?

814
01:07:58,094 --> 01:07:59,809
So some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) assumed that.

815
01:08:00,933 --> 01:08:02,283
But the Ayah(آية) ignored them.

816
01:08:04,382 --> 01:08:06,488
Yes, and then we'll take the Questions from there, it's one question here.

817
01:08:06,741 --> 01:08:25,353
Question From Audience.

818
01:08:25,377 --> 01:08:30,745
Tayyeb(طيب) the question is about the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ the best generation is my generation

819
01:08:31,233 --> 01:08:33,371
but then we know that there is a Hadith(حديث) that says that

820
01:08:33,695 --> 01:08:36,255
there will be, people will come at the end of time

821
01:08:36,295 --> 01:08:38,243
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They are my brothers

822
01:08:38,528 --> 01:08:43,223
and the effort of one of them is like the effort of 50 of you, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

823
01:08:43,949 --> 01:08:50,503
Now the general rule, is that the best generation were the earliest and then it goes down from there.

824
01:08:50,943 --> 01:08:53,934
That's the general rule, but there are exceptions to every rule.

825
01:08:54,510 --> 01:09:00,459
So the exception to that rule are Al-Mahdi(ألمهدي) and his followers,

826
01:09:01,246 --> 01:09:04,510
the 300 plus, who will follow him are in exception.

827
01:09:05,924 --> 01:09:09,672
The army that comes out from Aden(عدن) in Yemen, Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

828
01:09:10,112 --> 01:09:14,162
There's gonna be army of 12,000 that will come out Aden Abyan(عدن أبين)

829
01:09:14,548 --> 01:09:17,275
and they would give victory to this religion.

830
01:09:17,399 --> 01:09:19,880
And they are the best between me and them.

831
01:09:20,611 --> 01:09:23,012
They are the best between me and them.

832
01:09:23,955 --> 01:09:27,519
The exceptions are also some of the followers of Eesa عليه السّلام.

833
01:09:27,544 --> 01:09:28,985
There's in fact a narration,

834
01:09:29,296 --> 01:09:32,504
my Ummah(امة) is like rain, you don’t know where the benefit of it is?

835
01:09:32,540 --> 01:09:33,707
In the beginning or the end.

836
01:09:34,499 --> 01:09:36,797
All rain benefits, the beginning of it and the end of it.

837
01:09:36,940 --> 01:09:39,613
The beginning is Muhammadﷺ and the end is Eesa عليه السّلام.

838
01:09:41,188 --> 01:09:42,979
So there are exception to that rule.

839
01:09:45,023 --> 01:09:45,880
Yes brother!

840
01:09:46,149 --> 01:09:56,562
Question From Audience.

841
01:09:57,321 --> 01:10:05,232
Now, there is two opinions on whether his mother is relative of Khalid(خالد) or not.

842
01:10:05,331 --> 01:10:07,538
There is one view, is that she is cousin of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

843
01:10:07,610 --> 01:10:10,582
and the other view is that she is from Bannu Makhzoom(بنومخذوم), the family of Khalid(خالد).

844
01:10:10,655 --> 01:10:12,773
 However, whether they're relatives or not.

845
01:10:13,400 --> 01:10:16,235
There were physical resemblances between the two.

846
01:10:16,869 --> 01:10:21,104
Both were towering tall men, both were physically well built.

847
01:10:21,791 --> 01:10:24,511
And it is said but maybe this is an exaggeration,

848
01:10:25,149 --> 01:10:31,937
but it was mentioned that when they're sitting on their horses, their feet would touch the ground.

849
01:10:33,248 --> 01:10:38,659
Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم), they must be very tall, if that's true, but the two men were very similar.

